From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 04:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The lower screen's menu as the start menu (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

While the 3DS remaster's lower screen is its menu in the field, it is the
start menu. The start menu's task still runs everything (the apps its
buttons open, and the bag's and the party's uses that come back through
it), but its window is never drawn and its sprites are hidden; its input
is the lower menu's: up and down over the buttons that can be used, A, B
or X, and taps on the buttons.

- POKéMON, BAG, TRAINER, POKéDEX, SAVE and OPTIONS are the start menu's
  entries; MAP opens the Town Map (with the Town Map in the bag, where the
  bag can be used); POKéTCH closes the menu (the Pokétch is in the panel).
- The buttons that can't be used now are dimmed: the field says which
  every frame while the player could open the menu, the start menu when
  it opens.
- A tap on a button while the player could open the menu opens it
  straight on that button (field_control.c: as X does).
- Where the menu has an entry with no button (RETIRE in the Great Marsh
  and the Pal Park, CHAT in the Union Room), it's the DS's start menu on
  the upper screen, as before.
---
